  "notes": [
    "A source-only or host-only check MUST NOT set compiled guest PASS.",
    "The Java profile is only a closed-world already-completed int Future pipeline, not general task/async/lock support.",
    "Unsupported backends must reject task syntax before native guest artifact emission, not silently block or inline.",
    "The normative distinctions are: task<T> creates Future<T>; await task<T> spawns and joins; sync task<T> is inline on the caller; do sync task accepts void only, never aliases do task or discards nonvoid; verified cancellation and lock cleanup still require executed tests.",
    "Every backend requires exact-head compiler binary plus guest execution, cancellation race, reverse lock unwind, verified physical child retirement, and TenantVM isolation receipts."
  ],
  "hardening_notes": "These 11 additional task cases are immutable source-only admissions. Every backend must either execute its own guest positive and exact negative no-artifact errors or fail closed with an explicit unsupported-feature diagnostic, but may not claim cross-backend parity from this manifest. Original source profile blob/head snapshots are historical evidence anchors, not refreshed current-head certifications. Added 21 SHA-pinned TaskFuture target cases; each requires independent backend guest results or negative no-artifact receipts, with TaskCooperateRequest safe-point witnesses. Historical source profiles remain NOT_EXECUTED and must not be relabeled by this source-only matrix."
